# Code ownership → required review (ADR-EVO-01, Phase 83).
#
# The evolution framework's approval authenticity rests on this file PLUS branch
# protection: a change under /evolution/** (a prompt, the manifest, routing, agent
# specs) is a self-modification of the platform, so it MUST be reviewed and merged
# by a human maintainer — the runtime cannot verify a GitHub merge, it can only
# pin what the merged manifest declares (TITAN-EVO-001/002).
#
# OPERATOR ACTION REQUIRED: replace @titan-maintainers with your real GitHub team
# and enable "Require review from Code Owners" branch protection on the default
# branch, or this control is advisory only. `make check-evolution` additionally
# enforces that every manifest approval carries a real UUID approver + signed
# timestamp and that no prompt drifts from its pinned hash — but it cannot prove
# the approver *decided*; branch protection is what does that.

/evolution/**                 @titan-maintainers
/evolution/manifest.yaml      @titan-maintainers
.github/CODEOWNERS            @titan-maintainers
